            "message": {
              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "<revisionDecision>\n  <revise>yes</revise>\n  <issues>1. Unsupported addition: The draft mentions checking the satchel and the blizzard \"holding its breath,\" which are narrative flourishes but not strictly derived from the event outcome (bell ring). 2. Tone mismatch: The draft is overly dramatic (\"vibrate in your bones\", \"edge of the world\") for the requested I3-G2.5-S2.5-F3-U5 tone, which calls for relaxed, balanced, and idiosyncratic but not hyperbolic prose. 3. Repetition: The previous response already established the bell ringing and the environment; this draft repeats the setting description unnecessarily. 4. Concrete outcome fidelity: The event is a deterministic observation. The prose should focus on the sensory experience of the sound and the immediate surroundings without adding external dramatic weight.</issues>\n</revisionDecision>"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
